{
  "requirement": "The SDK interns the node data returned by `Domain::source_node` for the `OutlineData`. `Domain::node_content` returns that node’s contents. Mapping and read failures return errors. Agents use the node reference from discovery with `read_node`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover every obligation in `read_source.behavior`.\n\n**Interning the `Domain::source_node` result.**\n- `direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns` in `project_sources.rs` maps `source.txt` to \"source-node\" through the test domain's `source_node`.\n- It asserts that the recorded dependency is `Dependency::Node(intern_node(\"source-node\"), returned.fingerprint())`.\n- It also asserts that `read_nodes` equals `[\"source-node\", \"source-node\"]`, so the interned node data reached `node_content`.\n- `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` in `agent/tests.rs` covers several selectors (none, empty, `fn[chosen]`) and checks each resulting dependency.\n\n**`Domain::node_content` returns that node's contents.**\n- The direct-read test asserts `returned.format() == \"prepared contents\"`.\n- After the domain text changes, it asserts the record is no longer current.\n- `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` and `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` assert the delivered text and fingerprint values.\n\n**Mapping failures return errors.**\n- The direct-read test tries two failing addresses: `unknown.txt`, and `source.txt` with selector `line[unknown]`.\n- For both, `read_source` returns an error containing \"unsupported source item\".\n- The test then asserts that no dependency was recorded, that `reads == 0` and that `read_nodes` is empty. This shows the error happens before any content read.\n\n**Read failures return errors.**\n- With `fail_read = true`, the direct-read test asserts the error contains \"prepared source read failed\" and that no dependency is recorded.\n- A later successful read records exactly one dependency, so only successful returns are recorded.\n- `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` adds a missing-selector read (`fn[missing]`). It asserts that only the successful read contributes a dependency.\n\n**Agents use the discovery node reference with `read_node`.**\n- `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions` in `configured.rs` runs a scripted agent against a local HTTP server.\n- The agent calls `list_sources`, then `read_node` with the integer node taken from the listing. The test asserts that the text is \"a source snapshot\", which is the domain content. It also asserts that the on-disk \"selected disk contents\" is absent.\n- It then calls `read_node` with the node from a `search_text` hit.\n- `read_node` with `\"unknown\"` is rejected with \"invalid node ID\".\n- The test asserts the `read_node` schema takes an integer `node`, and that the dependency list includes the nodes read.\n- It runs the scenario twice, to cover independent executions.\n- `search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging` in `project_sources.rs` checks that a search hit's node reference, once chosen, yields the expected interned dependency and fingerprint.\n\nI found no obligation without a test and no assertion that contradicts the requirement. I read the test domain's `source_node` and `node_content`. They confirm that the error and content assertions exercise the mapping and read paths.",
  "references": "8dd8de79d0a6e3d8d5666c2c2e12294450569d5291c27a71be57931f922895b0",
